**Read:** [3D electromagnetic modelling and inversion — Oldenburg and colleagues](../sources/Open-Electromagnetic-Modelling-and-Inversion.lingua#r_5N6Z2MJVEW5GP1XW9J28J1AM69), entire paper, methods and one complete linked case; [Measuring Permittivity and Permeability — NIST TN 1536](../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91), complete applicable inversion and uncertainty methods.

Read the whole [3D electromagnetic modelling and inversion — Oldenburg and colleagues](../sources/Open-Electromagnetic-Modelling-and-Inversion.lingua#r_5N6Z2MJVEW5GP1XW9J28J1AM69), its linked complete reproducibility case and the applicable inversion/uncertainty parts of [Measuring Permittivity and Permeability — NIST TN 1536](../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91). Choose material reconstruction, source localization or a geophysical induction problem with explicitly available permitted data. Identify the measurement operator, unknowns, forward model and error assumptions.

First verify the forward calculation independently. Analyze its Jacobian, singular directions and parameter tradeoffs. Construct multiple plausible models, vary regularization/prior assumptions and compare the inferred result with actual data information. A posterior interval conditioned on one forward model does not include every possible model discrepancy.

Reproduce one published result in a separate exercise area without adding external datasets or notebooks to this repository. Then change geometry, calibration or a held-out frequency range and predict an independent observable. Explain what could not be identified and design the next measurement that would most directly resolve it. Compare a high-dimensional image with a simpler physically interpretable model. The scholarly depth is the argument from data and assumptions to a limited physical conclusion, not the apparent resolution of a reconstruction plot.

**Continue:** [An integrated electromagnetic-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN).

